From 849e00e3c28cf0c33617962dd177f92f9d31a899 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Christopher A. Williamson" <contact@chrisaw.io>
Date: Thu, 12 Mar 2026 21:02:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 7/8] Force PSI-based lmkd strategy on cgroup v2

Vendors with older Android 12 bases set ro.lmk.use_minfree_levels=true
which selects the legacy kill strategy requiring cgroup v1. On cgroup v2
(standard since Android 12), lmkd exits immediately with 'Old kill
strategy can only be used with v1 cgroup hierarchy'. Without lmkd,
ActivityManager cannot manage process lifecycle, causing cascading ANRs,
SystemUI failure, and boot timeouts exceeding 90 seconds.

Setting ro.lmk.use_new_strategy=true in system.prop forces PSI-based
monitoring regardless of vendor minfree_levels setting. This takes
effect before lmkd starts, unlike the rw-system.sh ro.config.low_ram
workaround which runs too late.
---
 system.prop | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/system.prop b/system.prop
index dd28057..b3e2224 100644
--- a/system.prop
+++ b/system.prop
@@ -55,3 +55,8 @@ vendor.usb.use_ffs_mtp=1
 ro.lmk.critical_upgrade=false
 # Kill heaviest task first for more predictable memory management
 ro.lmk.kill_heaviest_task=true
+# Force PSI-based kill strategy on all devices. Vendors with older kernels
+# may set ro.lmk.use_minfree_levels=true which selects the legacy cgroup v1
+# kill strategy. On cgroup v2 (standard since Android 12), this causes lmkd
+# to exit immediately, breaking process lifecycle management entirely.
+ro.lmk.use_new_strategy=true
-- 
